(5496430, 788802, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>First of all, let me congratulate you on getting twelfth place in this challenge, well done.<br/> <br/>I''ll be honest I gave this a 6.  Probably I was hovering between a 6 &amp; 7, but I think the blown out highlights did spoil it a little bit, so I ended up with a 6.<br/> <br/>The HDR is very well done, but has left the image with a slight soft feeling, as one of the commenters noticed.<br/> <br/>Overall I think this a good photo for the challenge. How lucky that you happened upon it within the right time frame.<br/> <br/>Sarah<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club First of all, let me congratulate you on getting twelfth place in this challenge, well done. I''ll be honest I gave this a 6.  Probably I was hovering between a 6 & 7, but I think the blown out highlights did spoil it a little bit, so I ended up with a 6. The HDR is very well done, but has left the image with a slight soft feeling, as one of the commenters noticed. Overall I think this a good photo for the challenge. How lucky that you happened upon it within the right time frame. Sarah ', '2009-05-22 12:55:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5496438, 790072, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I am sorry that this did not score better for you, I personally thought it was rather an interesting photo for this challenge. I suspect you knew that the abstract nature of the photo would probably not give you a very high score.<br/> <br/>The incredibly shallow depth of field is perhaps hurting you a little, as you know DPCers like things to be tack sharp.  I wonder if the chair is cropped a little bit too tightly, it maybe nice to see the chair in a bit more context.<br/> <br/>Overall though I liked the composition and abstract nature of the shot.  Only sorry it didn''t score higher for you.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club I am sorry that this did not score better for you, I personally thought it was rather an interesting photo for this challenge. I suspect you knew that the abstract nature of the photo would probably not give you a very high score. The incredibly shallow depth of field is perhaps hurting you a little, as you know DPCers like things to be tack sharp.  I wonder if the chair is cropped a little bit too tightly, it maybe nice to see the chair in a bit more context. Overall though I liked the composition and abstract nature of the shot.  Only sorry it didn''t score higher for you.', '2009-05-22 13:11:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5496502, 789935, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Technically this is a good shot, not blown out anywhere etc.  The composition is also good, and if it was a different challenge topic, I am certain it would have received higher scores.  However, I believe there is only really a tenuous relationship between the photo and the challenge topic.  Yes, it does have furniture in it, but is the furniture the main subject of the image, well, I don''t really think so.  Seems a bit of a shoehorn entry and I can''t help feeling this is why you received a sub five score.<br/> <br/>As I said, I think if you had this in a different challenge, then it may have scored better.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Technically this is a good shot, not blown out anywhere etc.  The composition is also good, and if it was a different challenge topic, I am certain it would have received higher scores.  However, I believe there is only really a tenuous relationship between the photo and the challenge topic.  Yes, it does have furniture in it, but is the furniture the main subject of the image, well, I don''t really think so.  Seems a bit of a shoehorn entry and I can''t help feeling this is why you received a sub five score. As I said, I think if you had this in a different challenge, then it may have scored better.', '2009-05-22 14:14:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5496982, 790105, 98339, '<td valign="top">what a fabulous idea!!! very well done!!!</td>', 'what a fabulous idea!!! very well done!!!', '2009-05-23 00:49:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5497056, 789906, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Technically I don''t see too much that is flawed with this image.  It''s in focus where it should be and the depth of field works well. <br/> <br/>I think the biggest problem, in terms of the low score you received for this challenge, is the fact the main subject is not really furniture, so you will have been hit with lots of DNMC votes.  <br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Technically I don''t see too much that is flawed with this image.  It''s in focus where it should be and the depth of field works well.  I think the biggest problem, in terms of the low score you received for this challenge, is the fact the main subject is not really furniture, so you will have been hit with lots of DNMC votes.   ', '2009-05-23 03:29:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5497058, 789621, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Sorry this did not score higher, I thought it was one of the more interesting images in this challenge. Also, check out the distribution of scores - that is really interesting.  No 9s or 10s and no 1s or 2s, then an almost even distribution of the other scores. Quite unusual I think.<br/> <br/>I love the composition, even though I''m sure this is a candid shot, it could conceivably have been a set up. The man looks so engrossed in his newspaper it is clear he is blissfully unaware that you have caught him.  Nice.<br/> <br/>I am a little unsure why this didn''t score higher, other than perhaps there was too much (or maybe not quite enough) of the canal boat showing.  Perhaps voters needed more context?  I don''t know, it certainly puzzles me.  I would have expected the score to be much closer to a 6.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Sorry this did not score higher, I thought it was one of the more interesting images in this challenge. Also, check out the distribution of scores - that is really interesting.  No 9s or 10s and no 1s or 2s, then an almost even distribution of the other scores. Quite unusual I think. I love the composition, even though I''m sure this is a candid shot, it could conceivably have been a set up. The man looks so engrossed in his newspaper it is clear he is blissfully unaware that you have caught him.  Nice. I am a little unsure why this didn''t score higher, other than perhaps there was too much (or maybe not quite enough) of the canal boat showing.  Perhaps voters needed more context?  I don''t know, it certainly puzzles me.  I would have expected the score to be much closer to a 6.', '2009-05-23 03:37:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5498002, 789938, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Congratulations on 10th place in this challenge!<br/> <br/>Great subject for the challenge, works really well, although I am wondering if this just happened to be out there in the middle of the countryside, or if you placed it there.  <br/> <br/>The composition is good, I particularly like the low perspective, but for me the processing spoils it a little.  There is a rather unnatural look, I assume coming from the use of the shadow/highlight function.  It leaves the sky particularly looking quite odd.  Sort of like using tonemapping, but not to the same extent.  (I know I never quite manage to get the sky right when using any kind of tone mapping/shadow/highlight adjustments).<br/> <br/>I gave this a 6 during voting, because of the processing.  Otherwise it would have been an easy 7 or even 8.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Congratulations on 10th place in this challenge! Great subject for the challenge, works really well, although I am wondering if this just happened to be out there in the middle of the countryside, or if you placed it there.   The composition is good, I particularly like the low perspective, but for me the processing spoils it a little.  There is a rather unnatural look, I assume coming from the use of the shadow/highlight function.  It leaves the sky particularly looking quite odd.  Sort of like using tonemapping, but not to the same extent.  (I know I never quite manage to get the sky right when using any kind of tone mapping/shadow/highlight adjustments). I gave this a 6 during voting, because of the processing.  Otherwise it would have been an easy 7 or even 8. ', '2009-05-24 07:30:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5498006, 788984, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Congratulations on 11th position.<br/> <br/>Difficult to give much helpful feedback on this one, as for me, this was actually one of my highest scoring images.  I think the composition is great, the editing works well for this, the only thing I wonder is perhaps the flash was too bright for this image?  Certainly I was rather surprised it did not score higher than it did.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Congratulations on 11th position. Difficult to give much helpful feedback on this one, as for me, this was actually one of my highest scoring images.  I think the composition is great, the editing works well for this, the only thing I wonder is perhaps the flash was too bright for this image?  Certainly I was rather surprised it did not score higher than it did. ', '2009-05-24 07:40:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5498358, 789985, 3746, '<td valign="top">Above and beyond the usual clichéd stuff we see on DPC - truly inspiring. well done. God knows how this didn''t break a 7.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-05-24 15:48:11.</i></td>', 'Above and beyond the usual clichéd stuff we see on DPC - truly inspiring. well done. God knows how this didn''t break a 7.', '2009-05-24 16:47:19.000000', '2009-05-24 16:48:11.000000', 0),
(5498484, 789810, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: a very good entry for this challenge.  Shows furniture and more importantly there is a story here.<br/> <br/>Technical: Great use of ambient lighting; dof good and composition is deceivingly simple but works very well. Like the filter you used, it seems to foreshadow a very long night ahead.<br/> <br/>Artistic: The slant and rigidity of your body drives home a sense of discomfort.  Love the tiny little blanket/shawl(?), it shows how you''re having to make do with what you can scrounge while the wifey gets all the good stuff! <br/> <br/>FWIW: Wouldn''t change a thing.  And you scored in the top 20 so good on you!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions.<br/> <br/>Susan<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: a very good entry for this challenge.  Shows furniture and more importantly there is a story here. Technical: Great use of ambient lighting; dof good and composition is deceivingly simple but works very well. Like the filter you used, it seems to foreshadow a very long night ahead. Artistic: The slant and rigidity of your body drives home a sense of discomfort.  Love the tiny little blanket/shawl(?), it shows how you''re having to make do with what you can scrounge while the wifey gets all the good stuff!  FWIW: Wouldn''t change a thing.  And you scored in the top 20 so good on you! Feel free to PM me with any questions. Susan', '2009-05-24 20:06:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5498493, 788882, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: ''Gee, looks like an opening shot for a scene from a SAW movie'' - and another commenter saw the resemblance too.<br/> <br/>Technical: Lighting is harsh and bleak, which works for this shot. Couch risks being lost in the midground; just barely below the dead centre of the shot.<br/> <br/>Artistic: Bleak industrial setting, fluorescent lighting, exposed pipes all juxtapose nicely with the unloved love seat, sitting there awaiting its fate. The dingy colour of the couch blends in very well with the overall scene.<br/> <br/>FWIW: I would have cropped out most of the foreground and pulled the couch further away from the wall on the left, to cast a longer shadow and give it a greater sense of isolation.  All in all good work, keep shooting!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: ''Gee, looks like an opening shot for a scene from a SAW movie'' - and another commenter saw the resemblance too. Technical: Lighting is harsh and bleak, which works for this shot. Couch risks being lost in the midground; just barely below the dead centre of the shot. Artistic: Bleak industrial setting, fluorescent lighting, exposed pipes all juxtapose nicely with the unloved love seat, sitting there awaiting its fate. The dingy colour of the couch blends in very well with the overall scene. FWIW: I would have cropped out most of the foreground and pulled the couch further away from the wall on the left, to cast a longer shadow and give it a greater sense of isolation.  All in all good work, keep shooting! Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-05-24 20:17:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5500051, 789938, 35720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by salmiakki:</b></div><hr/><i> Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Congratulations on 10th place in this challenge!<br/> <br/>Great subject for the challenge, works really well, although I am wondering if this just happened to be out there in the middle of the countryside, or if you placed it there.  <br/> <br/>The composition is good, I particularly like the low perspective, but for me the processing spoils it a little.  There is a rather unnatural look, I assume coming from the use of the shadow/highlight function.  It leaves the sky particularly looking quite odd.  Sort of like using tonemapping, but not to the same extent.  (I know I never quite manage to get the sky right when using any kind of tone mapping/shadow/highlight adjustments).<br/> <br/>I gave this a 6 during voting, because of the processing.  Otherwise it would have been an easy 7 or even 8. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks a lot Sarah for your good comment. I took this shot in a little phototrip to the countryside. I found this old chair in a abandoned house and placed it there in the nature. When I came home I had a very short time to edit before I had to submit. Thanks again.</td>', 'Originally posted by salmiakki: Greetings from the Critique Club Congratulations on 10th place in this challenge! Great subject for the challenge, works really well, although I am wondering if this just happened to be out there in the middle of the countryside, or if you placed it there.   The composition is good, I particularly like the low perspective, but for me the processing spoils it a little.  There is a rather unnatural look, I assume coming from the use of the shadow/highlight function.  It leaves the sky particularly looking quite odd.  Sort of like using tonemapping, but not to the same extent.  (I know I never quite manage to get the sky right when using any kind of tone mapping/shadow/highlight adjustments). I gave this a 6 during voting, because of the processing.  Otherwise it would have been an easy 7 or even 8.   Thanks a lot Sarah for your good comment. I took this shot in a little phototrip to the countryside. I found this old chair in a abandoned house and placed it there in the nature. When I came home I had a very short time to edit before I had to submit. Thanks again.', '2009-05-26 05:57:45.000000', NULL, 0),
